  "text": "Bees are small insects with a big job. They live together in a hive, and one hive has about fifty thousand bees. Every bee has work to do. Some bees clean the home. Some look after the babies. Others fly to flowers and drink sweet liquid called nectar.\n\nThey carry yellow powder from flower to flower. This helps new flowers and fruit to grow. The bees also make honey from nectar. Without bees, we have much less food. So please, be kind to bees!",
